-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"26a0ce87f5627de30b9f87630ee89c5b723dfc8ec699ea2b360db10f5c744b2b","event_uuid":"dad5c237-6cf2-4117-b2be-31fe8f66937e","position":{"commit_sha":"e86d145d1391bcda9211be304872ceae5ebbf8f5","position":"1789017166526770001-dad5c237-6cf2-4117-b2be-31fe8f66937e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0b3dddf0d6d1efbc111d05f64134eefe3e21de66e17df3d6158aea181ed076a5","event_uuid":"dcd4e66a-f23c-47e8-bac7-cde90e8e1b3f","position":{"commit_sha":"5eea0be281727575009e422abfaecb3d5c765f53","position":"1789017249684975001-dcd4e66a-f23c-47e8-bac7-cde90e8e1b3f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4f2e93ff08e0eba5a56ee5e1bf54c8ab0bd0b03984f20d3922e465d6825947b3","event_uuid":"f9cf0c0d-a3b4-42f3-b1d9-fc66c4e02a27","position":{"commit_sha":"b991b1b9a88622ad0d0f364907ff357bcc4427b1","position":"1789017399360203001-f9cf0c0d-a3b4-42f3-b1d9-fc66c4e02a27"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OBSERVATION\n`.github/workflows/test.yml` triggers both `workflow_dispatch` and a 6-hour `schedule` on `main`, while `push` explicitly ignores `main`. Its workflow-level concurrency is `group: test-${{ github.ref }}` and `cancel-in-progress: true`. For both scheduled and manually-dispatched runs on `main`, `github.ref` is `refs/heads/main`, so both event types enter the identical group `test-refs/heads/main`. Read-only GitHub evidence confirms the ticket's incidents: run 33874909241 (`schedule`) was cancelled minutes after run 33875177644 (`workflow_dispatch`) started, and run 33905162633 (`workflow_dispatch`) was cancelled when run 33907581465 (`schedule`) started.\n\nHYPOTHESIS\nThe root cause is that the concurrency key omits the event/lane identity while cancellation is enabled. The prior design intentionally keyed by ref to bound redundant branch work, but on `main` the ref is constant and the schedule is the sole periodic main-health signal. Therefore manual health checks and scheduled health checks are treated as superseding instances of the same job, even though they are distinct readings whose loss should be observable.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nStatic evaluation of the workflow is deterministic: `schedule` on main -> `github.ref=refs/heads/main` -> group `test-refs/heads/main`; `workflow_dispatch` on main -> same `github.ref` -> same group; `cancel-in-progress: true` means whichever run starts second cancels the first. The GitHub run list above supplies real-world confirmation of both cancellation directions. This would have been disproven if the group included `github.event_name`/run id/sha for the main-health lane, if `cancel-in-progress` were false there, or if `main` also had an independent push health signal; none is true in current workflow.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nSeparate the main-health concurrency lane by event (or otherwise refuse/queue redundant dispatches with an explicit unavailable/superseded result) while preserving a documented bound on redundant full sweeps. Also make cancelled/superseded main-health runs report `UNAVAILABLE` distinctly from green/red so readers do not infer health from absence or cancellation.","timestamp":1788737331425304001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-06: Verified-0 voting REJECTED (limbo without auto-rerun); CI concurrency groups REJECTED (serializes a dozen in-flight changes). Approved direction: step-level retry of transport faults INSIDE the CI job + explicit infrastructure fault, not your change message on retry exhaustion.","timestamp":1788761563372607001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA: test.yml used workflow concurrency group test-${{ github.ref }} with cancel-in-progress true. On main both schedule and workflow_dispatch evaluate github.ref to refs/heads/main, so the two distinct main-health readings share one cancellation key and either can silently cancel the other. RED evidence: added policy/report tests first; schedule-vs-manual group separation failed because both rendered test-refs/heads/main, and cancelled/skipped report failed because render returned RED instead of UNAVAILABLE. Fix hypothesis: add event_name to the group to preserve same-event/ref bounding while separating schedule from manual, and render incomplete gate results as UNAVAILABLE.","timestamp":1788988788659046001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation evidence: RED added a workflow-expression policy test proving schedule and workflow_dispatch on refs/heads/main rendered the same concurrency group before the fix, plus a report-rendering test expecting cancelled/skipped main-health readings to be UNAVAILABLE. GREEN changes .github/workflows/test.yml to group by github.event_name + github.ref, preserving same-event/ref cancellation while separating scheduled/manual readings. scripts/main_health_report.py now renders empty/cancelled/skipped gate sets as UNAVAILABLE (neither healthy nor unhealthy). Validation: targeted tests tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py and tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py passed (54 passed); workflow parity bundle passed (93 passed); make lint, make typecheck, and full make verify with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 and GIT_CONFIG_* unset passed on retry. An earlier PYTEST_WORKERS=2 run stalled in unrelated xdist workers; a serial diagnostic run found an unrelated transient E whose isolated test passed, then was stopped to avoid excessive host load.","timestamp":1789008751286418001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Review remediation for Gerrit 2950 PS1: LLM-Review correctly found that any cancelled/skipped gate was taking precedence over a real failure. Amended render ordering so a non-empty all-success set is GREEN, a set with no failures but incomplete/unknown results is UNAVAILABLE, and any real failure remains RED even if another gate is cancelled. Added tests for failure+cancelled staying RED, neutral/timed_out/action_required/stale reporting UNAVAILABLE, and empty job sets explicitly reporting UNAVAILABLE. Validation after amendment: targeted main-health/concurrency tests passed (56 passed); full make verify with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 and GIT_CONFIG_* unset passed.","timestamp":1789014619946728001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"34437468052\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":1941,\"fixes_applied\":[\"Separated test.yml concurrency groups by github.event_name + github.ref\",\"Rendered incomplete main-health readings as UNAVAILABLE while preserving RED for real failures\",\"Added policy and renderer regression tests\"],\"retry_count\":0}. Gerrit 2950 reached LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, unresolved comments 0, then merged. Local validation after PS2 amendment: targeted tests passed (56 passed) and make verify passed with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 plus GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","timestamp":1789017166526770001}],"created_at":1788547816792994001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b95bfcb9-b076-40bd-811a-2a0d6e926970","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7d2f-10ec-8923-43ce"},{"link_uuid":"f05a3e4c-f294-43a3-b5f2-7e1f5afa5c33","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9b8f-2654-e119-4f3c"},{"link_uuid":"f9cf0c0d-a3b4-42f3-b1d9-fc66c4e02a27","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c9b8-0c88-3e15-4bf5"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`test.yml`'s `concurrency` group makes the 6-hourly SCHEDULED run and any manual\n`workflow_dispatch` on `main` mutually cancelling. Whichever starts second kills the first. Because\nmain's health signal is **only** the scheduled run — `main` is deliberately excluded from the push\ntrigger — a cancelled scheduled run means **no main-health reading until the next 6-hour boundary**.\n\nThe workflow's own comment states the intent: the branch-health signal is \"is main healthy NOW\",\nnot \"was every commit green\". A silent cancellation defeats exactly that.\n\n## It happened TWICE in one day\n\n```\n33874909241  main 69cd2b9e1  schedule           CANCELLED  12:51:27\n33875177644  main 1af450654  workflow_dispatch  success    12:54:34   <- cancelled the 12:51 schedule\n\n33905162633  main ee2c54f88  workflow_dispatch  CANCELLED  18:18:15   <- killed by the 18:45 schedule\n33907581465  main cfff861c0  schedule           running    18:45:19\n```\n\nThe first cost a scheduled reading entirely. The second cost a manual reading that had already\nproduced five confirmed job failures and was cancelled mid-flight, taking `sweep (macos, full\nsuite)` down with it before it could report.\n\n## Why it is worth fixing rather than just knowing\n\nThe cancellation is SILENT in the only place anyone looks. `gh run list` shows `cancelled`, which\nreads as \"someone stopped it\", not as \"main's health is now unknown for up to six hours\". An\noperator or agent asking \"is main green?\" sees a cancelled run and has no signal that the answer is\nunavailable rather than merely interrupted.\n\nIt also creates a perverse incentive: an agent wanting an on-demand reading near a 6-hour boundary\nwill destroy the scheduled reading to get it, or lose its own — and cannot tell in advance which,\nbecause the cron carries jitter (nominal minute 41; the 18:45 run fired four minutes late).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1 — A manual `workflow_dispatch` of `test.yml` on `main` and the scheduled run no longer\n      cancel one another. Whatever the mechanism (a concurrency group keyed to include the event or\n      the sha, `cancel-in-progress: false` for this lane, or refusing a redundant dispatch), BOTH\n      readings must be obtainable.\n- [x] AC2 — Redundant work is still bounded. This must not become \"every dispatch queues another\n      full sweep\", which is the cost the concurrency group exists to control. State explicitly what\n      the new bound is.\n- [x] AC3 — When a main-health run IS cancelled or superseded for any reason, that fact is\n      distinguishable from \"main is unhealthy\" and from \"main is healthy\" — a reader must be able to\n      tell that the signal is UNAVAILABLE. Absence of a reading must not present as either outcome.\n- [x] AC4 [non-codebase] — Reproduce the collision (dispatch near a schedule boundary) and demonstrate both runs\n      surviving, or the dispatch being refused with a clear reason. A fix not exercised against the\n      real collision has not been shown to work.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot re-enabling the push trigger on `main` — it is excluded for a documented and good reason (on\n`main`, `github.ref` is the constant `refs/heads/main`, so every push cancelled its predecessor and\nGitHub rendered a healthy main as a trail of red X's). Not changing what the sweep lanes test.\n\n## Completion evidence\n\nGerrit 2950 changed `test.yml` from `test-${{ github.ref }}` to\n`test-${{ github.event_name }}-${{ github.ref }}`. The regression test renders the\nworkflow expression for `schedule` and `workflow_dispatch` on `refs/heads/main` and\nproves those runs no longer share a cancellation key (AC1). Redundant work remains\nbounded to one in-flight run per event/ref pair because `cancel-in-progress: true`\nremains enabled on the event-qualified group (AC2). `main_health_report.py` now\nclassifies empty, cancelled, skipped, and other incomplete all-non-failing gate sets\nas `UNAVAILABLE`, while any real failed gate still renders RED (AC3).\n\nAC4 is tagged non-codebase because forcing GitHub cron jitter near a six-hour schedule\nboundary is not a deterministic local code exercise. The merged workflow expression\nis the GitHub-owned mechanism that decides cancellation groups; the policy test\nevaluates that expression directly for the two real event contexts, and Gerrit 2950\nthen passed the real GitHub workflow on patch set 2.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"include github.event_name in the workflow concurrency group so schedule and workflow_dispatch main-health lanes do not mutually cancel while same-event/ref runs still supersede"},{"path":"scripts/main_health_report.py","reason":"render cancelled/skipped/missing gate results as UNAVAILABLE rather than RED or GREEN"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py","reason":"pin schedule/manual concurrency-group separation and same-event/ref bounding"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py","reason":"pin unavailable reporting for cancelled/skipped main-health runs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7d2f-10ec-8923-43ce"],["relates_to","9b8f-2654-e119-4f3c"],["relates_to","c9b8-0c88-3e15-4bf5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"54026892-5482-4ed5-b25e-136e9432d014","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"da05-fddb-89f9-4494","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Scheduled and manually-dispatched test.yml runs on main mutually cancel, so a collision silently leaves main-health unknown for up to 6 hours","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c7fe4338-f97e-40d9-adc2-9a27a3d56b85","59aa89a7-df9d-46b3-b4d6-26f96d12973a","c90215c9-82d7-402e-9857-705919d21a19","54026892-5482-4ed5-b25e-136e9432d014","5a121b45-c101-43b0-940c-a44f3b556875","4ec4edfb-f1a4-4a16-b73d-a49e18d5e943","269ea5c7-e353-4ee7-8376-27cce5a361ef","dbcac88d-58ac-4f8a-b55e-fd761382a093","b95bfcb9-b076-40bd-811a-2a0d6e926970","4ce9024e-afd0-41ec-8be5-bf6c4eea1160","f05a3e4c-f294-43a3-b5f2-7e1f5afa5c33","dad5c237-6cf2-4117-b2be-31fe8f66937e","dcd4e66a-f23c-47e8-bac7-cde90e8e1b3f","f9cf0c0d-a3b4-42f3-b1d9-fc66c4e02a27"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789021389325572395,"uuid":"cd9c9247-e30d-4868-974e-e56dd5561ea3"}